index=web sourcetype=access_combined
| rex field=_raw "\"(?<http_method>[A-Z]+)\s+(?<request_path>\S+)\s+HTTP/[^\"]+\"\s+(?<http_status>\d{3})"
| where request_path="/checkout" AND http_status>=500
| stats count by request_path, http_method, http_status
| sort -count

I received a request to investigate checkout failures on an e-commerce website.
I would start by searching Apache access logs for checkout requests returning HTTP 5xx errors. 
I would then review the affected requests and error patterns to help identify the problem.
